[{:working/title "Google Workspace ingest — operator-action handoff", :working/id "gworkspace-ingest-operator-handoff-260513", :working/last_verified "2026-05-13", :working/status "active", :working/body "\n# Google Workspace ingest — operator-action handoff (2026-05-13)\n\nPhase-0 blockers that the agent has resolved + the residual manual steps the operator must execute.\n\n## Status snapshot\n\n| Blocker | Resolution | Path |\n|---|---|---|\n| (1) RW migration `20260507850000_vertex_gworkspace_oauth_tokens` | ✅ **already applied** on Vultr RW (`45.32.79.245:4566`). Stale `172.236.132.11` ETIMEDOUT note in `deps.toml` resolved. 8 `vertex_g*_oauth_token` tables verified live. | n/a |\n| (4) Per-service `sync_from_google()` impl | ✅ **rewired**. Bodies always existed in `pymagatama/ingest/{drive,contacts,tasks,docs,sheets,slides,meet}.py`; previously dead because `zeebe_worker_main.py:6881` routed everything to the `gworkspace_lite` stub. Fixed at lines 4223–4234 + 6899–6903. | `pymagatama/zeebe_worker_main.py` |\n| (2) GCP Console redirect URIs | ⏳ **manual** — operator must paste 8 URIs into Google Cloud Console OAuth client. | §GCP Console step |\n| (3) Per-account OAuth consent | ⏳ **manual** — browser round-trip per (account × service). Walker script provided. | §Consent walker |\n| (5) Worker image rebuild + helm upgrade | ⏳ **manual** — re-build `ghcr.io/gftdcojp/pymagatama:*` then `helm upgrade` the default-profile worker so the rewire is in production. | §Deploy |\n| (6) k8s Secret bind for SS_GOOGLE_OAUTH_* | ⏳ **manual** — confirmed via `kubectl get deploy -A -o json` that no deployment currently has `SS_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` / `SS_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET` env. CF Secrets Store holds them but pyzeebe pods run on Vultr K8s, not Workers. Need a k8s Secret + envFrom on the worker deployment. | §Deploy |\n\n## (2) GCP Console redirect URIs\n\nConsole: <https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials> → project **ai-gftd-ws-ingest** (under `jun@gftd.group`) → OAuth 2.0 Client ID `96227025012-…`.\n\n`gmail.gftd.ai/oauth/callback` is already registered. Add the remaining **8** entries (note: `calendar.gftd.ai` callback still returns 404 — its Worker also needs redeploy, see §Deploy):\n\n```\nhttps://calendar.gftd.ai/oauth/callback\nhttps://drive.gftd.ai/oauth/callback\nhttps://contacts.gftd.ai/oauth/callback\nhttps://tasks.gftd.ai/oauth/callback\nhttps://docs.gftd.ai/oauth/callback\nhttps://sheets.gftd.ai/oauth/callback\nhttps://slides.gftd.ai/oauth/callback\nhttps://meet.gftd.ai/oauth/callback\n```\n\nSave. No client_secret rotation required.\n\n## (3) Per-account OAuth consent\n\n**Important**: the deployed CF Workers for drive/contacts/tasks/docs/sheets/slides/meet currently expose only `/oauth/callback`, not the `ai.gftd.apps.<svc>.connectAccount` XRPC procedure (returns SvelteKit 404). The walker therefore **constructs the Google consent URL locally** instead of round-tripping through XRPC. Only the callback round-trip needs the Worker, and that route is live for all 7 services. (`calendar.gftd.ai/oauth/callback` returns 404 — see §Deploy.)\n\n11 Google accounts discovered in 1Password (`70-tools/scripts/google-accounts-from-1p.sh`):\n\n```\ncontact@oikos-technologies.com\ncontact@rokes.exchange\nhello@ouchi.earth\nhello@rokes.exchange\nj.kawasaki@de.school\njk@michael.ne.jp\njun.kawasaki@edutek.company\njun@gftd.group                       ← Workspace primary (gftd.group tenant)\njun784@gmail.com\nroot@jk.luxury\nroot@junkawasaki.com\n```\n\nConsent is **one screen per (account × service)**, but Google remembers the account choice within a browser session so each subsequent service is a 2-click confirm. With the unified 12-scope grant, the first service per account is a single multi-scope consent screen, then 7 quick re-grants for the remaining services.\n\nRun the walker (sequentially per account, all 9 services, opens browser tabs):\n\n```bash\n./70-tools/scripts/gworkspace-consent-walker.sh <email>\n# Examples:\n./70-tools/scripts/gworkspace-consent-walker.sh jun@gftd.group\n./70-tools/scripts/gworkspace-consent-walker.sh root@junkawasaki.com\n# ...repeat for all 11 accounts\n```\n\nEach tab redirects to `https://{service}.gftd.ai/oauth/callback?code=…&state={accountDid}` → CF Worker → `{service}.oauthCallback` Zeebe task → `vertex_g{service}_oauth_token` row (refresh_token KEK-enveloped). Re-running the walker for the same account is idempotent (upsert by `vertex_id = \"{accountDid}|{email}\"`).\n\nVerify after each account:\n\n```bash\nexport PG_URL=\"$(op item get yi7hc5wozgfhbaneb3ny46w6ua --fields label=password --reveal)\"\npsql \"$PG_URL\" -c \"SELECT 'gdrive' AS svc, email, status, last_sync_at FROM vertex_gdrive_oauth_token\nUNION ALL SELECT 'gcontacts', email, status, last_sync_at FROM vertex_gcontacts_oauth_token\nUNION ALL SELECT 'gtasks',    email, status, last_sync_at FROM vertex_gtasks_oauth_token\nUNION ALL SELECT 'gdocs',     email, status, last_sync_at FROM vertex_gdocs_oauth_token\nUNION ALL SELECT 'gsheets',   email, status, last_sync_at FROM vertex_gsheets_oauth_token\nUNION ALL SELECT 'gslides',   email, status, last_sync_at FROM vertex_gslides_oauth_token\nUNION ALL SELECT 'gmeet',     email, status, last_sync_at FROM vertex_gmeet_oauth_token\nORDER BY svc, email\"\n```\n\n## (5) Deploy\n\nThe pyzeebe-worker rewire (blocker 4) lives in the current branch but the running default-profile worker image is older. Four things to do:\n\n1. **Create k8s Secret for Google OAuth credentials** (currently NOT set on any deployment — verified via `kubectl get deploy -A -o json | grep SS_GOOGLE`):\n\n   ```bash\n   # Fetch values from GCP Console (or from CF Secrets Store dashboard) and create:\n   kubectl create secret generic gworkspace-oauth -n intel \\\n     --from-literal=SS_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID='96227025012-nnvmf7l8rfmttdrag3tkqnl51eg2lnpq.apps.googleusercontent.com' \\\n     --from-literal=SS_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET='<from GCP Console / wrangler secrets-store metadata says ID=2611e1b0485047d6a09fdf434037a9b9>'\n\n   # Patch deployment to envFrom the secret\n   kubectl set env deploy/intel-pyzeebe-worker -n intel --from=secret/gworkspace-oauth\n   ```\n\n2. **Rebuild pymagatama image**:\n\n   ```bash\n   cd 20-actors/magatama/py\n   # follow whichever image-build flow the deps.toml mailer profile uses\n   # (latest tag pattern: pymagatama:<profile>-<yymmdd>[suffix]-amd64)\n   ```\n\n3. **Helm upgrade**:\n   - `intel-pyzeebe-worker -n intel` runs default profile (no `ZEEBE_WORKER_PROFILE` env) and is the natural consumer of `{drive,contacts,tasks,docs,sheets,slides,meet}.{connectAccount,oauthCallback,syncFromGoogle,cronTick}`. **However it is currently failing to reach `zeebe-gateway.mitama-udf` (`Socket closed` retry loop)** — see `_working/malak/surveillance/PYZEEBE-REDEPLOY-HANDOFF.md`. Fix the gateway connectivity first, then `helm upgrade` with the new image tag.\n   - Alternative: bring up a dedicated `gworkspace` profile worker (mirror of the `mailer` profile block).\n\n4. **Calendar CF Worker redeploy**: `calendar.gftd.ai/oauth/callback` returns 404 even with a `code` param; the deployed bundle is older than `60-apps/ai-gftd-project-calendar/.../src/app.ts:35`. Redeploy via `gftd deploy` from that directory before adding the calendar redirect URI to GCP Console.\n\n## After-action: cron schedule\n\nOnce tokens are live and the worker is running:\n\n- BPMN definition `ai.gftd.gworkspace.cronTick` (or wherever the scheduler lives) fires `{service}.cronTick` every 15 min — each invocation calls `cron_tick()` which picks the 10 oldest active accounts per service and runs `sync_token()` (Drive `changes.list` cursor / Tasks `updatedMin` / Contacts `syncToken` / Meet `conferenceRecords.list filter=start_time>=` / Sheets+Slides+Docs via Drive cursor).\n- Initial backfill per account: depending on Drive size, expect **multiple cron cycles** before `last_sync_at` stabilizes (cursor-resumable, no risk of duplication thanks to `WHERE NOT EXISTS (vertex_id)` guard in `_insert()`).\n\n## Deps.toml correction (pending)\n\n`deps.toml [[migrations]] google-workspace-ingest-phase0` checklist has multiple items that the live cluster shows as already done. Should be updated to reflect:\n\n- `[x] Migration 20260507850000 apply` (was `[ ]`)\n- `[x] drive worker 初回 deploy` (was `[ ]` — Worker is live and `/oauth/callback` returns 400-on-missing-code)\n- `[x] All 7 service syncFromGoogle wired to pymagatama T2 ingest` (deps.toml claims only sheets/slides done; in reality all 7 are now wired)\n- `[ ] GCP Console redirect URI for calendar/drive/contacts/tasks/docs/sheets/slides/meet` (still open per this runbook)\n- `[ ] Per-account OAuth consent` (still open)\n", :working/doc_type "how-to", :db/id -1, :working/authoritative false, :working/topic "gworkspace-ingest"}]